Subject: [PATCH 3/8] fix(hooks): Make pre-commit-format run on bash 3.2

The hook opened with `declare -A`, an associative array builtin that bash 4
introduced. macOS ships bash 3.2, and settings.json invokes the script as
`bash ~/.claude/hooks/scripts/pre-commit-format.sh` rather than through the
shebang, so the builtin was never available.

Under `set -euo pipefail` that failed on line 8, before any formatting ran.
The hook is wired to `Bash(git commit*)` and fails closed, so the effect was
not a skipped format step but a blocked commit: no commit issued through
Claude Code could run at all, and `just format` never executed pre-commit.

Replaces the map with two "<hash> <path>" snapshots compared by line. Paths
containing spaces still round-trip, because a git hash never contains one.

